Track 1: “Did You Salt the Melting Block?”
- Story & Context: When Sector 7’s central coolant line ruptured into the communal kitchen facility of the Cheongna deep-bunkers, chef-turned-vocalist Mina watched forty gallons of ancestral beef broth freeze solid in seconds, locking her family’s prized marrow bones in industrial ice. Jin-Woo patched a field recorder into the cracking ice shelf while Mina rested her cheek against the stainless steel preparation table, matching her shivering vocal scales to the twelve-beat-per-minute cardiac tempo of a brumating polar bear broadcast on the bunker’s emergency wildlife channel. As the synth lead moaned like an uninsulated boiler pipe losing its last steam, Mina sang into an iced-over phone receiver: "Tell me how the broth forgets the flame when the frost drinks first."
