Track 2: Sora at the Rations Table
- Story & Context: Written during a fourteen-day blackout in the sub-level residential wards, this confession track documents Sora, a logistics clerk who secretly diverted the bunker’s emergency butter and dried chilies to her lover’s dormitory. The music barely stirs above a rhythmic coma, its bass dropping like blood through stiffened capillaries every four seconds while Sora’s vocals murmur against an analog lead synth that weeps and bends like warping plastic. In the freezing gloom, the song captures the exact sensation of scraping cold chili paste with wooden chopsticks while listening to a neighbor’s failing chest unit down the hall: "I kept the tallow soft under my tongue just to speak your name warm."
