Track 3: Cast-Iron Skillets Swallowing Frost
- Story & Context: The final track records the mythic morning the underground inhabitants finally opened the blast doors to find the above-ground district buried beneath an unbroken, mirror-flat sheet of pale blue glacial crust. In the abandoned rooftop dining pavilion, rows of forgotten cast-iron cookware had collected snow blooms that refused to melt over the portable butane burners, an image Jin-Woo scored using a glacial modular synth solo that slides between notes without ever landing on a stable pitch. Mina recorded the vocal hook in a single take without headphones, letting her naturally decelerating, hypothermic breath pattern sculpt the gaps between the subterranean bass thuds: "Leave the feast upon the iron, let the winter eat what we became."
